  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 31. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 奇術 — 仕掛けや技で不思議に見せる芸。\n2. 傷口 — 皮膚などが傷ついたところ。\n3. 絆 — 人と人の間にある強いつながり。\n4. 季節風 — 季節によって主な向きが変わる風。\n5. 北側 — 北に当たる側。\n6. 北口 — 建物や駅などの北側にある出入口。\n7. 北国 — 北の方にある土地や国。\n8. キック — 足でボールなどを蹴ること。\n9. キックオフ — サッカーなどで試合を始めるためにボールを蹴ること。\n10. キット — 何かを作るための部品などを一そろいにしたもの。\n11. 切符 — 乗り物などを利用できることを示す券。\n12. 吉報 — うれしい知らせ。\n13. 汽笛 — 船や機関車などが合図に鳴らす笛。\n14. 機内 — 飛行機の中。\n15. 記入 — 決まった欄などに必要なことを書くこと。\n16. 絹糸 — 蚕の繭から作る糸。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
